+	<script>
+		// foul-play-ish-aok offline fix: scripts/mirror-sprites.js only
+		// mirrors *static* per-species battle sprites (the "gen5" family),
+		// not animated GIFs -- but Dex.getSpriteData() (battle-dex.ts)
+		// prefers an animated sprite whenever animation metadata for the
+		// species is available, which it always is once data/pokedex-mini.js
+		// and data/pokedex-mini-bw.js are loaded, regardless of Pokemon
+		// generation or the "2D sprites instead of 3D models" (bwgfx)
+		// setting -- BattlePokemonSpritesBW's animated entry gets tried
+		// either way. That's true by default (the "noanim"/"nogif" prefs
+		// are both null/off out of the box), so every in-battle sprite
+		// request 404s. PSPrefs reads its stored prefs from
+		// localStorage["showdown_prefs"] synchronously in its constructor,
+		// which runs the moment js/client-main.js is parsed below -- so
+		// this has to seed that key before that script tag.
+		//
+		// This only ever sets noanim specifically, not the whole
+		// showdown_prefs blob: an earlier version of this fix bailed out if
+		// showdown_prefs already existed *at all*, which meant it silently
+		// did nothing for anyone who'd ever changed any other setting
+		// (theme, layout, ...) -- that write already puts a showdown_prefs
+		// object in localStorage with no "noanim" key in it, which isn't
+		// the same thing as the user deliberately choosing to re-enable
+		// animation. Checking for the "noanim" key specifically, and
+		// merging into whatever's already stored, fixes sprites for that
+		// case too without touching any other saved preference. If the
+		// user (now or later, via the "Disable animations" checkbox) ever
+		// does set noanim explicitly, that choice is respected and never
+		// overwritten here.
+		try {
+			if (window.localStorage) {
+				var storedPrefs = {};
+				try { storedPrefs = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('showdown_prefs')) || {}; } catch (e) {}
+				if (!('noanim' in storedPrefs)) {
+					storedPrefs.noanim = true;
+					localStorage.setItem('showdown_prefs', JSON.stringify(storedPrefs));
+				}
+			}
+		} catch (e) {}
+	</script>
